# =============================================================================
# FILE: .dockerignore
# PURPOSE: Optimize Docker Build Context & Prevent Sensitive Data Leaks
# =============================================================================
#
# ARCHITECTURAL RATIONALE:
#   When `docker build` runs, the entire local directory context is serialized
#   and transmitted to the Docker daemon. Excluding non-essential assets achieves:
#     1. Build Speed: Prevents transmitting hundreds of megabytes of local data.
#     2. Image Layer Caching: Ensures changes to tests, docs, or local caches
#        do not invalidate Docker layer cache hits.
#     3. Zero Secret Leakage: Prevents local .env files, private credentials, and
#        debug logs from accidentally baking into production container layers.
#     4. Cross-Platform Stability: Prevents local host-compiled binary artifacts
#        (e.g., node_modules or Python venvs compiled on Windows/macOS) from
#        polluting the Linux Alpine/Debian container environment.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Version Control Metadata
# Prevents repository history (.git) from leaking into the container filesystem.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Host-Specific Dependencies & Virtual Environments
# Dependencies must be resolved and compiled cleanly inside the target Linux container.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv
venv
ENV/
env/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Local Environment Variables & Secrets
# CRITICAL SECURITY: Production secrets must be injected at runtime via
# Google Cloud Secret Manager or Cloud Run Environment Variables.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
*.crt
id_rsa*
service-account*.json
credentials.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Testing Artifacts, Code Coverage & Linting Configurations
# Testing suites and coverage reports are unnecessary inside production runtime layers.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage
.nyc_output
*.test.js
*.spec.js
*.test.ts
*.spec.ts
jest.config.*
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Developer IDE & Operating System Artifacts
# Cleanly strips host workstation clutter.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Documentation & Build Scaffolding
# Keeps the build context restricted strictly to deployable source files.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
LICENSE
docs/
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
